# ── UX4G generated assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are produced by scripts/build-ux4g-assets.mjs from the pinned
# ux4g-web-components package, which npm install already brings in. They are
# build output, not source:
#
#   * the stylesheet is ~773 kB of generated CSS
#   * the fonts are ~2.3 MB of binary lifted out of that CSS
#
# Committing them would put three megabytes of derived bytes under review on
# every UX4G bump, and would let the checked-in copy drift from the package the
# lockfile pins. The Docker build runs `npm install` and then `prebuild`, so the
# image regenerates them itself and still reaches no network at runtime.
src/design-system/tokens/ux4g.generated.css
src/design-system/tokens/ux4g.generated.manifest.json
public/assets/fonts/ux4g/
